      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## MiniMax H3 masked video inpainting\n\n1. Upload a **24 fps** source video containing an audio track.\n2. Upload or paint a mask image. **White regenerates; black preserves.** One mask image is broadcast across the full video.\n3. Edit the H3 prompt to describe the intended replacement inside the mask.\n4. Queue the workflow.\n\n**Trim Source AV** drops trailing frames to the largest valid `17k+5` length and trims audio to the same 24 fps duration. Its `h3_length` output controls H3 conditioning.\n\nThe resized source frames feed the video VAE and the 32×32 grid preview. Replace the static mask with **SAM3 Track to Mask** for a moving temporal mask. Grid Preview shows one selected frame but its snapped-mask output contains the complete batch.\n\n**Apply Target Mask** attaches the spatial mask to the real encoded source AV latent. This example preserves the complete source audio. The node activates native H3 masks—or the bundled compatibility—automatically; no MODEL patch node is required.\n\nThe source video belongs in the sampler target latent. Do not also connect it as an H3 video reference merely to make inpainting work."
      ],
      "title": "How to use this workflow",
      "color": "#222",
      "bgcolor": "#000"
    },
